<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Huahine</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1895 CE (approx.) · capital Fare</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A kingdom of the Leeward Society Islands that defeated a French landing in 1846 and stayed independent until the 1890s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huahine">Huahine</a>, two islands joined by a narrow channel in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands-society-islands">Leeward group</a> of the Society Islands, was settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesians">Polynesians</a> perhaps a thousand years ago. Around Lake Fauna Nui at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeva">Maeva</a>, its chiefly families built one of the largest concentrations of marae in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>. By the 18th century the island and nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maiao">Maiao</a> were ruled by a single royal line.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huahine">Huahine's</a> ruling family was closely tied by marriage to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-tahiti">Kingdom of Tahiti</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teriitaria-ii">Teriitaria II</a>, queen from 1815, was also a wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-cook">James Cook</a> visited in 1769 and in 1777 left the traveller Mai, who had been to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, settled there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> arrived in 1818 and most islanders became Protestant. Islanders lived from breadfruit, taro, fishing and provisioning ships.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1846 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huahine">Huahine's</a> warriors defeated French marines who tried to impose a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarnac-convention">Jarnac Convention</a> of 1847 recognised its independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> proclaimed annexation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands-society-islands">Leeward Islands</a> in 1888, completed on Huahine in 1895, and it is now part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-polynesia">French Polynesia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-huahine.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Huahine" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Bringing It All Back Home · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Huahine.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1895 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fare</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Teriitaria II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Polynesian religion, later Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tahitian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Huahine and Maiao</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=kingdom-of-huahine" aria-label="Kingdom of Huahine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="570 2799 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Huahine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M890 3055L938 3085"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M938 3085h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M890 3055h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M890 3055h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fare. <a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=kingdom-of-huahine">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
